{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows","id":1353218,"title":"The After-shock war, in the Age of Sorrows","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-06T19:37:58-08:00","id":1353218,"title":"The After-shock war, in the Age of Sorrows","content":"Many thanks to Omicron of SB, whom I cant seem to contact<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forums.spacebattles.com/threads/general-exalted-debate-third-edition-actually-2nd.263244/page-44#post-12209803\" target=\"_blank\">https://forums.spacebattles.com/thre...#post-12209803</a><br /> <br /> And to Dr. Love Monkey. Who was so helpful.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>So what was the divergence? </b></span><br /> <br /> The first age chugged along, far from war and conflict and pain. Nothing interrupted it. Brigid died in a sorcerous experiment, seeking out a new spell. Then the Usurpation occurred, and all was silent. The Solar Essences were bound, placed within the Jade Prison, and then hidden. The Lunars fled, the Dragonblooded took over, and the Sidereals retreated to Heaven.<br /> <br /> The Rametheus came.<br /> <br /> Perhaps if the Solars were here, they could have stopped him. Perhaps if the Exalted Host worked as one, instead of a dozen disparate factions squabbling and fighting, perhaps they could have seen him first. Perhaps if the infrastructure of the shogunate had been preserved, instead of torn down by squabbling daimyos and irate Lunars, they could have survived. Perhaps if Dragonblooded had posted outposts and had worked together to protect creation, instead of sucking jade out of Creation and focusing on their own pleasures, they could have realized they were under attack. But they didn't, and so doom befell them all.<br /> <br /> The first to realize were the Yozis. With the Unconquered Sun deep in the games, the Sidereals overworked, and no Solars to summon their third circles, nobody realized what the Yozis knew. Rametheus sent an envoy to them, speaking of freedom. Of hope. Of a second chance. Screams and roars came out, but the Yozis, once exiled, agreed assistance. The Deathlords, hearing orders for the first time from their Neverborn masters, came out to assist. There were only a few things left to do.<br /> <br /> First was the destruction of the Exalted Host<br /> <br /> Second, was a secret.<br /> <br /> It started small. A Lunar or so disappeared. A village or two went silent. Slowly, ever so slowly, the things beyond the Blessed Isle went silent. The abilities of the Sidereals were studied, read, and analyzed, and countermeasures were developed to take advantage. The Lunars were picked off, one by one, either taken over by doppelgangers in a mockery of their own abilities, or simply rendered silent. Entire villages were taken over. Forests in the east were rendered into crystal for the new war. Shadowlands were depopulated of ghosts, fettered by devas and forced to learn necromancy. Cults surged. A dozen emissaries flitted from kingdom to kingdom, setting up strife and war between all. Within heaven, infiltrators were unleashed. Hundreds of dispossessed gods, starving and desperate for a handout... it was all too easy.<br /> <br /> Too late, they realied what was happening. Assassins were dispatched, slaying Sidereals and gods alike, using weaknesses and loopholes provided by desperate gods. Cults beckoned first and second circle demons, unleashing them upon Creation, forcing the Wyld Hunt and the Lunars to fight. And even then, it didn't stop, false flag attacks forcing Dragonblooded and Lunar Exalted to fight against one another, Immaculate propaganda and specialized second and third circles forcing them to fight against one another when they should have fought on the same side. The Realm was paralyzed. Dragonblooded, seeking power for their own houses and damning everyone else, had taken bribes and had found themselves corrupted and in a web of blackmail and desperation.<br /> <br /> Rametheus, struck, again and again. Hitting the wounded, striking at the people the Lunars loved most, hitting at Dragonblooded infrastructure. The armies of the Dragonblooded commanders died, not to devas or sorcery, but to disease. Cities which gave out supplies to the armies in the threshold were annihilated the moment the Dragonblooded turned their backs on it by sorcereies such as River of Blood and Cantantas of empty voices, forcing them to split their forces or simply evacuate as the mortals were slain by their tens of thousands. Iron-Skinned-Defender, Lunar, was killed as he tried to protect his people, surrounded from all sides and kept from fleeing by the threat of killing his entire clan. Necromancy raised the ghosts of Sidereals, Dragonblooded, and Lunars, choking out the secrets of Creation's defenders from them. In one portion of the threshold, the skies were darkened by sorcery, and entire armies of zombies marched out, lead by the Mask of Winters, to pillage and consume all that stood in their way.<br /> <br /> With a shudder, the Sidereals realized what was happening. They studied the archives plundered by the traitor gods and studied what was left of their Sidereal compatriots' ghosts. And realized that Rametheus was searching for the Jade Prison. Perhaps he wanted to destroy the Solar Essences once and for all. Perhaps he simply wished to corrupt them to free the Yozis. Whatever he wanted, it couldn't be allowed.<br /> <br /> That was when Rametheus attacked Yu-Shan. The Celestial Lions grunted as they were cut down by an army of Devas, as the armies of Rametheus, the garden of war, marched into Yu-shan. A portion of the Sidereals ran to defend Heaven. Another portion went to stop them from finding the Jade Prison. And another portion betrayed them all, revealing themselves to be Akuma. By this time, half the Sidereals had been slain, killed by ambushes set around fate disruptions.<br /> <br /> On the Blessed Isle, the Sword of Creation fired, again and again and again, each blast slewing tens of thousands of the invaders, but all the while, destroing the blessed isle's geomancy. Entire manses went dark. Fields of crops were turned to dust by the power pushed. And cracks began to appear, as thousands of years of misuse and lack of maintenance lead to the great weapon of creation slowly breaking. The Dragonblooded Host now, at long last, fought as one. Lookshy and Gem and The Realm and Outcastes and everyone else, fighting off incursions by second circle demons, peasant uprisings spurred on by the honeyed words of puppet-devas, and worse.<br /> <br /> In the end, Rametheus found the Jade Prison, despite the Sidereals' precautions, and arrived there. Only to be met by the combined host of Dragonblooded, Lunars, and Sidereals, and the last Solar remaining. The Aerial Legion was deployed, marching upon the host of Rametheus and the demons that have been set loose into Creation proper. The Jadeborn moved there, the last pieces of their artifacts present within the host. There, battle raged on, even as a portion of the Elders of the Exalted Host carried out their last plan.<br /> <br /> Rametheus could not be allowed to take the solar exaltations. Rametheus could not be allowed to exterminate the human race. Rametheus could not be allowed to win. But the Solars were gone, and even if they were here, fighting an entire primordial with zero preparation and support from Autochthon and the Unconquered Sun would be suicide.<br /> <br /> There was only one last thing to do. Exaltations could not be destroyed, but there was a use in sacrifice. And as Rametheus crushed the throat of Chejop Kejack, letting his corpse fall to the ground, it looked up, and beheld the destruction of reality. The Fae, watching from the sidelines, screamed as the felt Order calcifying them. The loom of fate twisted, strained, and snapped, and finally, broke. And the sun shone, through the darkness, as Creation was reordered. And, most importantly of all, the Sidereals realized just what Rametheus wished to do. The Exalted could do the impossible, and so Exaltations must be denied to the enemy. All of them. Lunars, Solars, Sidereals, bound themselves into the Jade Prison, and cast it beyond Time and Space, so not even the rogue primordials could find them. <br /> <br /> It was like the Time of Cascading years... but not like it. Time, for the first time since the primordial war, warped, as the past was rewritten and re-ordered. Tens of thousands of worlds, all with a different timeline and a different plane of existence. Between the worlds of man, was the world of the Wyld, Yu-Shan, and the Underworld. Each with their own separate pasts, each with their own separate destinies. And each with their own human populations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 09-16-2020, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T17:30:54-08:00","id":1354011,"title":"","content":"This is awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T18:11:30-08:00","id":1354019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1354011#post1354011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Finally. Someone commented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T16:23:47-08:00","id":1354482,"title":"","content":"Go too far outside of the scope of conversation in a forum and people have no idea how to respond to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T16:45:29-08:00","id":1354488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1354482#post1354482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go too far outside of the scope of conversation in a forum and people have no idea how to respond to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait. Alternate shards are outside scope?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T11:19:34-08:00","id":1354621,"title":"","content":"So Yu-Shan, Creation, and the Underworld are like alternate universes of each other now? Slight differences but the same people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T12:24:24-08:00","id":1354644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uknown DarkLord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1354621#post1354621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Yu-Shan, Creation, and the Underworld are like alternate universes of each other now? Slight differences but the same people?</div> </div> </div> </div>The alternate universe part? Only for Creation. <br /> <br /> Its like... imagine a place. A building, if you will, that is divided like the spokes of the wheel. Each spoke, is a separate alterante universe. If you want to get to another spoke? You gotta cross over. Either between spokes, or enter the central hub. Yu-shan is something else. A bubble of elsewhere, a long dead city. But you can use the Wyld or Underworld, each representing the space in between the spokes. And each spoke? It's most definitely different. They all have human souls. But that's... mostly it. Some of them have history where they don't have access to thaumaturgy or sorcery. Others don't even have gods or elementals. Some have history thousands of years long, others millions of years. Some have a creation myth where they were made by the gods. Others evolved from apes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T12:26:08-08:00","id":1354645,"title":"","content":"Assuming I actually get around to running a game in 2020, I may steal part of this for the plot. I love the stealthy campaign of sabotage and assassination leading up to the full invasion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T12:31:49-08:00","id":1354648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1354645#post1354645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming I actually get around to running a game in 2020, I may steal part of this for the plot. I love the stealthy campaign of sabotage and assassination leading up to the full invasion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. You can grab a bunch of demons from... the link. Assuming you can contact Omicron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T15:22:14-08:00","id":1355504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1354488#post1354488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait. Alternate shards are outside scope?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's just a theme I've noticed over the years. Go too far out of what people want to talk about regarding a particular RPG, you get crickets. I've posted a couple alternate ideas over the years and was surprised how little attention some of them get.<br /> <br /> Mage:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/775036-an-au-mono-paradigm-mage-owod\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/775036-an-au-mono-paradigm-mage-owod\"> An AU-Mono Paradigm Mage oWoD - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/775036-an-au-mono-paradigm-mage-owod\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/775036-an-au-mono-paradigm-mage-owod </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Ok. So based on my prior two threads I've been doing some deep thinking on a Harry Potter-ish style AU WoD for mage. This is for a solo game with my wife, who </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> or <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/391931-cwod-without-any-supernaturals\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/391931-cwod-without-any-supernaturals\"> cWoD without any Supernaturals? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/391931-cwod-without-any-supernaturals\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/391931-cwod-without-any-supernaturals </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> What would happen to the cWoD if, say, circa 1945, the end of WW2, something happened that wiped out about 99.9% to 99.999% of all supernatural* beings in the cWoD? I was only ever an M:tA and V:tM player back in the day, and am not sure what kind of repurcussions would be felt over time. The reason I ask </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> I posted about Solars reappearing before the Empress dissapears:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1190751-what-if-all-the-solars-were-released-before-the-disappearance-of-the-empress\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1190751-what-if-all-the-solars-were-released-before-the-disappearance-of-the-empress\"> What if all the Solars were released before the disappearance of the Empress? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1190751-what-if-all-the-solars-were-released-before-the-disappearance-of-the-empress\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1190751-what-if-all-the-solars-were-released-before-the-disappearance-of-the-empress </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Idle thought here, what would happen if the Jade Prison was destroyed before the Empress disappeared? Edit: I'm thinking... say 300 years before her official </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I see I got 25 replies, at the time I was sure I would have gotten more interest. I think when an idea is also something a lot of other people have thought about, you get a lot of interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T05:10:36-08:00","id":1355614,"title":"","content":"I'm curious how the initial campaign of sabotage and assassination could be interactive.<br /> I've played a DotFA game where the Solar Deliberative was being destroyed by a seemingly invincible enemy and getting reports of dead exalts like it was an afternoon weather report was pretty disheartening. It was like War of the Worlds with the added pressure that we were going to have to be the ones to turn this whole thing around somehow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T05:22:19-08:00","id":1355616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1355614#post1355614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious how the initial campaign of sabotage and assassination could be interactive.<br /> I've played a DotFA game where the Solar Deliberative was being destroyed by a seemingly invincible enemy and getting reports of dead exalts like it was an afternoon weather report was pretty disheartening. It was like War of the Worlds with the added pressure that we were going to have to be the ones to turn this whole thing around somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess you can be playing as a dragonblooded investigator. Trying to root out the truth. After all, Ramethus is going to try and weaken creation first. Which means making all the dragonblooded houses are at one another's throats. It probably won't last for long, but the expended resources would be useful.<br /> <br /> Or someone like a... Lunar. On the border marches. Some fucked up shit is happening. Kingdoms are at each other's throats. Cults are rising. And several Lunar elders are found dead. And now, something is hunting you, the ultimate predator. Will you escape? <br /> <br /> Or as a Sidereal. Currently, your compatriots are slowly disappearing. Someone is laying ambushes and murdering them. But whom?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T14:07:11-08:00","id":1356690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1355614#post1355614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious how the initial campaign of sabotage and assassination could be interactive.<br /> I've played a DotFA game where the Solar Deliberative was being destroyed by a seemingly invincible enemy and getting reports of dead exalts like it was an afternoon weather report was pretty disheartening. It was like War of the Worlds with the added pressure that we were going to have to be the ones to turn this whole thing around somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind explaining some more? That sounds fascinating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":". 12-23-2019, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T10:02:48-08:00","id":1356813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1355614#post1355614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious how the initial campaign of sabotage and assassination could be interactive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's probably best if it's not interactive. Session 0 is explain the premise of the game. Session one opens with Star Wars style floating text &quot;It is a dark time for Creation. Though the Exalted have won the Primordial War, Creations kingdoms find themselves on the brink of a globe spanning war as the most powerful and influential world leaders are assassinated by an unknown force. Our heroes have rallied in Nexus to try to hold together the fragile peace, as their enemy moves against them in the shadows...&quot; <br /> <br /> Start the PCs too early in the plot and you risk them blowing the lid too soon (or even killing your Primordial if you play fair). Either that or you risk rail-roading them (&quot;I know you rolled 33 successes, but you fail anyway because this is only session 2&quot;).<br /> <br /> Better to just narrate that the world is on the brink and let them have at it.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to actually play that part, I think Accelerator's ideas are solid. I'd say that if we're doing sneaky misdirection, destabilization, assassination, then there's probably plenty of proxies, cat's paws and red herrings. Run it almost film noir style: courtly intrigue mixed with stalking the mean streets for hired killers. Maybe set it up to look like it's a Deathlord behind it all, then pull a big reveal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T18:28:54-08:00","id":1356871,"title":"","content":"I took a stab at statting out a Jotun assault form for Rametheus.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Essence: 10; Willpower: 10; Join Battle: 12 dice (Base 7)<br /> Personal Motes: 150<br /> Health Levels: -0x30/-1x30/-2x30/-4x20/I<br /> Actions: Stealth 15 dice, Senses 15 dice, Resist Poison/Disease 14 dice, Feats of Strength 20 dice (Rametheus meets all strength requirements)<br /> Combat<br /> Attack (Tool of War): 18 dice (Damage 26, minimum 10)<br /> Attack (Tool of War, Arrow): 18 dice at Short range (Damage 26, minimum 10)<br /> Grapple: 16 dice (14 dice to control)<br /> Combat Movement: 16 dice<br /> Evasion 7, Parry 7<br /> Soak/Hardness: 25/12<br /> <br /> <i>Offensive Charms</i><br /> <br /> <b>Lightning War Essence</b> (5m; Reflexive; Instant): Rametheus knows to strike second is to not strike at all. After all join battle rolls have been made at the begining of a combat, if Rametheus does not have the highest initiative, it may activate this charm. Roll a number of dice equal to the difference between Rametheus's initiative and the highest initiative in the combat with double 7s, for each success Rametheus gains a point of initiative.<br /> <br /> Any attacks Rametheus makes in the first round of combat add bonus dice to the attack equal to the initiative gained.<br /> <br /> <b>Protection Dismantling Touch</b> (3m; Supplemental; Instant, Decisive-Only): When Rametheus hits a target with a decisive attack or successful gambit supplemented by this charm, roll 5 dice. For each success Rametheus may end the duration of a charm or spell on the target. This effect takes place before damage is rolled.<br /> <br /> <b>Withering Titan Grip</b> (5m; Supplemental; Instant): This charm supplements a grapple by granting double 8s on the control roll. If successful Rametheus need not use an action to savage the held target, but may do so reflexively once on each of its turns. Rametheus may maintain any number of grapples supplemented by this charm. <br /> <br /> <b>The Greatest Weapons</b> (10m 1wp; Simple; Instant): Rametheus unleashes a miasma of disease and poison. All enemies within Long range must immidiately roll to resist the Venom of Rametheus and the Plague of Conflict. Enemies who are not aware of Rametheus at the time suffer a -2 penalty to both rolls. Rametheus may choose to supress either the poison or disease at its descretion.<br /> <br /> This charm is usable once per combat unless reset by slaying a creature who is suffering from both disease and poison.<br /> <br /> <b>Abhorrance of Half Measures </b>(5m; Supplemental; Instant): Rametheus may add up 5 successes to any action, or raise any static value by 5.<br /> <br /> <b>Genesis of Movement</b> (8m; Reflexive; Instant): Rametheus takes three actions on it's turn instead of one. Rametheus may not flurry for more actions.<br /> <br /> <i>Defensive Charms</i><br /> <br /> <b>Infinitely Adaptable Titan Form</b> (3m; Reflexive; One Tick): Rametheus's form constantly adapts to new foes and new avenues of attack. For one tick all onslaught penalties add to defense, instead of subtracting from it. Any onslaught penalties applied while this charm is active fade at the end of the tick.<br /> <br /> <b>Twisting Space Counterassault </b>(7m 4i; Reflexive; Instant; Counterattack, Perilous): When Rametheus is attacked it may respond with this charm, making a decisive counter attack before damage against it is rolled. If the attack hits it uses the target's initiative value to determine damage, and returns the target to base initiative. If the damgage is sufficient to increase the wound penalty of the target, the target's attack is cancelled.<br /> <br /> Note that if Rametheus has been targetted with a decisive attack, then the damage or gambit is then resolved with the target's base initiative.<br /> <br /> <b>Smoke and Vapor Elusion </b>(10m 1wp; Simple; Instant): As quickly as Rametheus strikes, so too does he fade. After activating this charm Rametheus rolls to disengage with five automatic successes. If successful Rametheus retreats beyond the borders of Creation.<br /> <br /> <i>Miscellaneous Charms</i><br /> <br /> <b>Materialize</b> (75m, 1wp; Simple; Instant): Rametheus may materialize as its form emerges from an obscuring cloud of smoke. If Rametheus is forced to materialize against its will, it does so for free.<br /> <b>Terror of Night</b> (1wp; Simple; Scene): Rametheus slips past guards and wards like sand through fingers. For the duration of the scene Rametheus doubles 8s on stealth rolls and is always treated as having full cover for the purposes of hiding, even when in a wide open and brightly lit area. These effects also apply to any demons Rametheus has brought with it to the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Feast of Blood</b> (10m; Simple; Indefinite): Rametheus may regenerate itself, feeding on the conflict of others. When Rametheus activates this charm it falls into a deep sleep. While asleep Rametheus can draw life from violent death around it. If any sapient creature loses its life in a violent way within Extreme range of Rametheus, it regains a health level.<br /> <br /> Merits<br /> Will of the Titans: When Rametheus spends a willpower to add a success to an action it gains two successes rather than one.<br /> <br /> Protean Arsenal: Rametheus's tools of war are treated as having access to any weapon tag it desires, such as two-handed or piercing.<br /> <br /> Ten Thousand Forms: At the begining of each round Rametheus may change it's size, choosing to take on or drop either the Miniscule Size, Tiny Creature, or Legendary Size merits. Rametheus is also immune to the effects of mundane poisons and diseases.<br /> <br /> Corporeal Unbinding: Rametheus may strike immaterial creatures as though they were material, and may strike material creatures even while immaterial.<br /> <br /> <b>Entourage</b><br /> Rametheus's body is the size of an entire world and populated by a variety of demons that it will bring with it to battle. In dire circumstances it's assault Jotun may even attack with several third circle souls supporting it, each equal in power to the Jotun in their own ways.<br /> <br /> Venom of Rametheus:<br /> Damage: 4i/round (L in Crash), Duration 10 rounds, Penalty -5<br /> <br /> Plauge of Conflict:<br /> Virulence 6, Morbidity 6, Interval: One Day)<br /> <br /> Minor Symptom: The victim becomes irritable and unsatisfied, treating all intimacies of compassion and cooperation as one level lower.<br /> <br /> Major Symptom: Once per day, at the Storyteller's discretion, the character must disagree with a course of action proposed. The character must then persue their disagreement until victory is achieved, even if it progresses to violence. They may end this effect by spending a willpower and calling on a Major or Defining intimacy.<br /> <br /> Defining Symptom: The character becomes completely insufferable. Every scene where she is expected to work with others, she must either spend a willpower and call on a Defining intimacy, or achieve some sort of social or physical victory over the people she is working with, with a preference for bloodshed.<br /> <br /> Death: At last the bloodlust overwhelms the victim, and they throw themselves into battle until they die, even against allies. If their dearest companions are the only ones available to battle then the character may take their own life to spare them.<br /> <br /> Storyteller Tips<br /> Rametheus is deadly, but also intelligent. It only sends its assault jotun into battles that it knows it can win, or deal terrible damage and then retreat. It is also utterly savage and ruthless, incapacitating the weaker warriors first, and then fighting the strong until it is no longer safe to do so. If it can, it will launch the first attack as an ambush. If it suffers too much damage in the assault it slips into a populated but weakly defended area of Creation and uses The Greatest Weapons to infect them all with the Plague of Conflict, and then Feast of Blood to quickly regenerate its health.<br /> <br /> There are ways to weaken it, however. Many of the charms and abilities listed here can be sabotaged by performing specific actions within the world body of Rametheus, and in other places in Creation.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T15:48:41-08:00","id":1366416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1356690#post1356690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind explaining some more? That sounds fascinating.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sorry, at the time I had this whole post planned but got distracted.<br /> <br /> Essentially this wasn't the game that we were promised. I'd made a Night Caste called Radiant Mya who was supposed to be a social infiltrator rather than a ninja assassin. I'd deliberately given her quite low Dexterity in favour of high socials so she could charm her way into places she shouldn't be able to and worked for a secret society that considered IAM a terrifying intrusion into people's privacy.<br /> <br /> So we'd had this rival who'd seemingly killed our previous circle despite a significant age/power disparity and the first part of the game involves my discovery that he was an Akuma. He then attacks us with everything and he's defeated with ease despite the fact he'd apparently killed our previous incarnations and the new circle only really had the Dawn and Zenith who could be called combatants. <br /> <br /> That's when they came! Cyclopian mole people with some kind of power to adapt to/negate essence. If you were fighting them then your charms incurred this building mote surcharge and they had the ability to poke through essence based deceptions like Myas. This caused a scenario where she was revealed in the middle of the enemy camp and the sheer lack of combat ability or weapons led to her throwing a shoe at someone in desperation.<br /> <br /> What really soured me on the premise was realising how often things were being fudged for us to not die while at the same time getting nowhere. I'm 90% sure in retrospect that the Storyteller was in a depression spiral and was running us into an unbeatable enemy as a reflection of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T21:55:49-08:00","id":1367392,"title":"","content":"The question is, should I have the Unconquered Sun die? I mean, he's constantly suppressing Temperance to play the games of Divinity? Rametheus could have simply smashed his way into the jade pleasure dome, and jabbed the sword of the yozis at his face, and he probably wouldn't raise a hand to defend himself. <br /> <br /> On one hand, its a good way to show how things cannot be brought back. On the other hand, it seems like a sucky way to die for the King of the Gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T22:16:27-08:00","id":1367398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367392#post1367392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question is, should I have the Unconquered Sun die? I mean, he's constantly suppressing Temperance to play the games of Divinity? Rametheus could have simply smashed his way into the jade pleasure dome, and jabbed the sword of the yozis at his face, and he probably wouldn't raise a hand to defend himself.<br /> <br /> On one hand, its a good way to show how things cannot be brought back. On the other hand, it seems like a sucky way to die for the King of the Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also awesome for the players if you're going by 2e rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T22:37:59-08:00","id":1367399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367392#post1367392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question is, should I have the Unconquered Sun die? I mean, he's constantly suppressing Temperance to play the games of Divinity?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how it worked in 2e. Suppressing a virtue only kept it down for a scene, even if the behavior that ran counter to the virtue lasted for far longer than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-13-2020, 01:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T22:42:50-08:00","id":1367400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367399#post1367399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not how it worked in 2e. Suppressing a virtue only kept it down for a scene, even if the behavior that ran counter to the virtue lasted for far longer than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Really? <br /> <br /> Then I should have Rametheus grab someone or carry out some plot that forces the Sun to suppress Temperance. Let's see... suppressing Temperance would mean that he either lies, breaks his promises, or indulges. So there's the Games of Divinity, so I must make him break his promise. <br /> <br /> What about a promise to keep someone or something safe, and then Rametheus holds it hostage, forcing him into a no-win situation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T22:48:13-08:00","id":1367401,"title":"","content":"I mean, even <i>without</i> his Temperance, the Unconquered Sun could still weather even a pretty impressive attack and kill Rametheus in one hit with his spear.<br /> <br /> \u200b(And no, I don't know what the weakness in Rametheus' perfect defense is. But Iggy D should, considering the millennia he spent with Rammy as one of his multitude of dickhead bosses.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T23:00:04-08:00","id":1367405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367401#post1367401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, even <i>without</i> his Temperance, the Unconquered Sun could still weather even a pretty impressive attack and kill Rametheus in one hit with his spear.<br /> <br /> \u200b(And no, I don't know what the weakness in Rametheus' perfect defense is. But Iggy D should, considering the millennia he spent with Rammy as one of his multitude of dickhead bosses.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like how... <br /> <br /> You know what? Fuck it. I'm too tired for this shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T23:17:47-08:00","id":1367407,"title":"","content":"Look, all I'm saying is, just kicking in the door and attacking the Unconquered Sun is not a smart move. Rametheus should be smart enough to know that the Unconquered Sun isn't a pushover even with one or more of his Virtues down, and that his retaliation will be swift and possibly lethal to even one as mighty as a Primordial.<br /> <br /> Heck, him attacking the Unconquered Sun in the first place is actually what drops his protection <i>against</i> attack by the Unconquered Sun. As long as <i>that's</i> up, the Geas prevents Conky from throwing his godspear at the guy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T23:35:23-08:00","id":1367409,"title":"","content":"Maybe.... But i still want the sun dead.<br /> <br /> Ramethus can have a perfect defense that functions during combat and then basically throw a dozen chips, betting on being able to murder the unconquered sun. <br /> <br /> It means that solars no longer have any patron to give them nice messages, neither is there any more big good in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T00:12:47-08:00","id":1367411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367409#post1367409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ramethus can have a perfect defense that functions during combat...</div> </div> </div> </div><i>All</i> perfect defenses function during combat. But they're generally supposed to have some vulnerability. In the case of Primordials, the vulnerability was something thematic to them - Cecelyne's were vulnerable to attacks that could strike dematerialized spirits; Malfeas' only functioned inside places designed to be lived in; the Ebon Dragon's failed against Holy attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367409#post1367409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bBut i still want the sun dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you can do that. But it's probably gonna require a more complex strategy than just kicking in the door of the Jade Pleasure Dome and putting a sword in the guy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-13-2020, 03:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T00:28:23-08:00","id":1367412,"title":"","content":"I apologize.<br /> <br /> What I meant was... Well, it's Ramethus. The Garden of War. <br /> <br /> What kind of vulnerability would he have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T01:07:50-08:00","id":1367419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367412#post1367412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apologize.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I didn't mean to ruffle your feathers, either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367412#post1367412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I meant was... Well, it's Ramethus. The Garden of War.<br /> <br /> What kind of vulnerability would he have?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. <i>Some</i> vulnerability. Nobody's perfect. Since you're the one fleshing this scenario out, perhaps you should come up with a flaw of invulnerability for Rammy's perfect defenses?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T01:14:08-08:00","id":1367425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367419#post1367419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you. I didn't mean to ruffle your feathers, either.<br /> <br /> I don't know. <i>Some</i> vulnerability. Nobody's perfect. Since you're the one fleshing this scenario out, perhaps you should come up with a flaw of invulnerability for Rammy's perfect defenses?</div> </div> </div> </div>*sigh*<br /> <br /> I'm sorry again. Text is horrific for putting in tone. That was basically a rhetorical question. The thing is, since this is Rametheus, the Garden of War, what I'm thinking is that its some kind of, well, perfect that works with it. Rametheus is a being that cannot be defeated in the kind of combat he likes. Or at least, he's the primordial that pared himself down into the epitome of battle and war. <br /> <br /> In other words, if he was to break the jade pleasure dome to bits and then stab the sword of the yozis at Sol's face? I say that his perfect is the exact kind of thing that works in that scenario. To beat him, you have to steal the initiative. You'll have to, I dunno, surprise attack him, or hit him before he hits you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T01:18:56-08:00","id":1367429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367401#post1367401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, even <i>without</i> his Temperance, the Unconquered Sun could still weather even a pretty impressive attack and kill Rametheus in one hit with his spear.<br /> <br /> \u200b(And no, I don't know what the weakness in Rametheus' perfect defense is. But Iggy D should, considering the millennia he spent with Rammy as one of his multitude of dickhead bosses.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Can the Unconquered Sun, or any god for that matter, even fight against a Primordial ? Since they created the Exalted to fight the enemies they could not fight themselves, I assumed all the gods had a sort of geas that prevents them from fighting the Primordials themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T01:19:28-08:00","id":1367430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367429#post1367429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can the Unconquered Sun, or any god for that matter, even fight against a Primordial ? Since they created the Exalted to fight the enemies they could not fight themselves, I assumed all the gods had a sort of geas that prevents them from fighting the Primordials themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently there's a thing in 2e that says 'A primordial attacking a god means the god can fight back'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T01:26:33-08:00","id":1367435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367429#post1367429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can the Unconquered Sun, or any god for that matter, even fight against a Primordial ? Since they created the Exalted to fight the enemies they could not fight themselves, I assumed all the gods had a sort of geas that prevents them from fighting the Primordials themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2e, which is where they fleshed out the Geas, the Geas only functioned so long as the Primordial in question didn't attack the god in question.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn 3e this hasn't been covered, and honestly I prefer it that way. We're way into the metaphysics weeds, here.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T01:34:13-08:00","id":1367440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367435#post1367435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 2e, which is where they fleshed out the Geas, the Geas only functioned so long as the Primordial in question didn't attack the god in question.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn 3e this hasn't been covered, and honestly I prefer it that way. We're way into the metaphysics weeds, here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I wasn't talking about a mechanical rule, but more about &quot;The Primordial Age was terrible for the gods because their creator could bring their end arbitrarily and they couldn't even try to resist&quot; kind of things","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T01:38:11-08:00","id":1367442,"title":"","content":"I mean, I don't consider Donald Trump's presidency to be a terrible time for Americans because I'm worried he can just show up out of nowhere and punch me and I can't hit him back. I consider it terrible because he's casually dismantling systems and endangering the things I love as he strides thoughtlessly around the country like it's his personal playground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T01:40:21-08:00","id":1367443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367442#post1367442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I don't consider Donald Trump's presidency to be a terrible time for Americans because I'm worried he can just show up out of nowhere and punch me and I can't hit him back. I consider it terrible because he's casually dismantling systems and endangering the things I love as he strides thoughtlessly around the country like it's his personal playground.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but a specific point that marked me in the Primordial Age description is that the gods couldn't even rebel. Even the Unconquered Sun had to pass his strength onto others so they could fight injustice because he couldn't on his own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T14:33:00-08:00","id":1367607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367405#post1367405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean like how...<br /> <br /> You know what? Fuck it. I'm too tired for this shit.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Careful. You just got back from a suspension.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-13-2020, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T15:18:37-08:00","id":1367627,"title":"","content":"So, as someone who's killed the Sun a couple of times. Let's rap.<br /> <br /> Frankly, all of the Sun's toys are... a pain.<br /> <br /> You can do it by knocking down Temperance and (2E) spaming stunted perfects. But I strongly recommend getting that damn spear.<br /> <br /> How?<br /> <br /> Engineer a crisis that challenges the Sun on multiple fronts. This is easier if you have his ear in Heaven. We convinced him to give The Bull his Spear. This doesn't stop him simply recalling the Godspeed Reflexively, but we had him in a position where doing so would lead to the deaths of everyone in White Wall (and therefore mean suppressing Compassion). Then we challenged him to a fist fight (so what if my fists have One Hand Fury), so recalling the Spear would mean suppressing Valor as well.<br /> <br /> Still... if you wanted some kind of blitz... Why stop at the Sun?<br /> <br /> Why not take out all of The Heavenly City? Do Primordial shenanigans to cast all Yu Shan into the Deep Wyld, forever separated from Creation? Basically kills all the Celestines (maybe a facet of Luna survives, Maidens as required). Cuts off the Sids. I could see some Primordial war machine doing that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T15:28:22-08:00","id":1367631,"title":"","content":"I wonder if you threw them far enough away or segmented then enough if that might deactivate all of the celestial exaltations in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T16:30:06-08:00","id":1367642,"title":"","content":"I don't think so; it's power they've invested permanently in their champions, not something that requires them to be around per-se.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T20:30:12-08:00","id":1367677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367631#post1367631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if you threw them far enough away or segmented then enough if that might deactivate all of the celestial exaltations in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Celestial exaltations are independent of their patron. Killing the sun just makes solars angrier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T20:56:05-08:00","id":1367679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367677#post1367677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Celestial exaltations are independent of their patron. Killing the sun just makes solars angrier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, but what if you threw them to the other side of Oramus or something, like to the point where it unmakes them ever having existed in the world. It could snap creation around and have them lose every exalt type except for DBs and some of the new ones. I think even Exigents would be out of luck since their power comes from the Sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T21:41:39-08:00","id":1367681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367679#post1367679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yes, but what if you threw them to the other side of Oramus or something\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Oramus is in the Demon City. Demons walk from one side of him to the other on a daily basis, probably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T21:55:45-08:00","id":1367684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367681#post1367681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oramus is in the Demon City. Demons walk from one side of him to the other on a daily basis, probably.</div> </div> </div> </div>What am I thinking of then? The space where things go when they never were?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T22:21:38-08:00","id":1367688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367679#post1367679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, yes, but what if you threw them to the other side of Oramus or something, like to the point where it unmakes them ever having existed in the world. It could snap creation around and have them lose every exalt type except for DBs and some of the new ones. I think even Exigents would be out of luck since their power comes from the Sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rewriting history is a shaping attack. Exaltation, and exalts, are immune to those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T22:41:06-08:00","id":1367691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367688#post1367688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rewriting history is a shaping attack. Exaltation, and exalts, are immune to those.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, you might be able to do something with them though. The Jade prison is a thing that happened. Also the Lunars altered their castes from age to age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T23:27:19-08:00","id":1367695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367691#post1367691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, you might be able to do something with them though. The Jade prison is a thing that happened. Also the Lunars altered their castes from age to age.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. But note, you can't destroy them. And no matter what happened, you can't deal with the fact that exaltation requires free will. <br /> <br /> In other words, exaltation will always be there. Always existing. By all means, lock them away in the deepest, darkest dungeon and throw away the key. There's always the chance they'll get out. And they'll be waiting there for one more spark of heroism to ignite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T23:32:45-08:00","id":1367696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367684#post1367684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What am I thinking of then? The space where things go when they never were?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you talking about putting something beyond the boundaries of one or more of the shinma? Because that\u2019s not something you can do just by throwing really hard.<br /> <br /> To put it a little more simply, the shinma are just a flowery way of saying some really obvious stuff about reality and the stuff inside reality (things can exist; things can be identified; things can be in places; things can interact with each other; things cannot be perfect; things can come into conflict with each other) by showing the \u201cthings\u201d that <i>don\u2019t</i> follow those rules (Nishkriya cannot come into conflict with anything; Dharma is perfect and unchanging; Nurvikalpa cannot interact with anything; Nirupadhika cannot be anywhere; Nirvishesha has no identity; Nirguna does not exist).<br /> <br /> Very fitting when talking about what some Fair Folk believe. Less useful when talking about stuff taking place anywhere near Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-14-2020, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T02:43:01-08:00","id":1367715,"title":"","content":"I believe he means The Beyond, like what happened to Prince Laashe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T04:38:12-08:00","id":1367724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367695#post1367695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yup. But note, you can't destroy them. And no matter what happened, you can't deal with the fact that exaltation requires free will. <br /> <br /> In other words, exaltation will always be there. Always existing. By all means, lock them away in the deepest, darkest dungeon and throw away the key. There's always the chance they'll get out. And they'll be waiting there for one more spark of heroism to ignite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily, the Exaltations are bound to Creation and Humans. If you get rid of those that\u2019s pretty well the end of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T04:39:11-08:00","id":1367725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367715#post1367715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe he means The Beyond, like what happened to Prince Laashe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may actually not be thinking god anything from exalted. Maybe from Warhammer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T04:51:55-08:00","id":1367727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367724#post1367724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not necessarily, the Exaltations are bound to Creation and Humans. If you get rid of those that\u2019s pretty well the end of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. You can render exaltation useless by making the human race extinct. Good luck with that though. <br /> <br /> But for the purpose of this discussion (trying to undo the derail here) humanity isn't extinct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T06:18:51-08:00","id":1367736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367727#post1367727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course. You can render exaltation useless by making the human race extinct. Good luck with that though. <br /> <br /> But for the purpose of this discussion (trying to undo the derail here) humanity isn't extinct.</div> </div> </div> </div>No but considering the nature of Exaltation that\u2019s probably a good first step for Rametheus. Maybe it starts by going around wiping out the more isolated and least defended populations first while stoking the fires around the Solar-Lunar-Dragonblooded conflicts. It could probably even enlist some real solid help from the Deathlords and their minions. Maybe even get a hold of the Sword of Creation and shoot it until it breaks.<br /> <br /> I think somewhere it\u2019s said the Sword is capable of destroying all of creation if used that way so you\u2019re pretty good there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T07:56:11-08:00","id":1367760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367736#post1367736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No but considering the nature of Exaltation that\u2019s probably a good first step for Rametheus. Maybe it starts by going around wiping out the more isolated and least defended populations first while stoking the fires around the Solar-Lunar-Dragonblooded conflicts. It could probably even enlist some real solid help from the Deathlords and their minions. Maybe even get a hold of the Sword of Creation and shoot it until it breaks.<br /> <br /> I think somewhere it\u2019s said the Sword is capable of destroying all of creation if used that way so you\u2019re pretty good there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, rest assured, its quite likely that Rametheus goes around throwing 2nd and 3rd circle diseases around for shits and giggles, because well, he's out to play for keeps. It's just that.... Exalted are really hard to kill, and odds are that any exalted who survive would try their best to revive the human race. Dragon blood is so dispersed amongst the human population that pretty much everyone has it, and Lunar and Sidereal exaltations are indestructible and there's no way to catch them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 02-14-2020, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T08:14:14-08:00","id":1367764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367760#post1367760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh no, rest assured, its quite likely that Rametheus goes around throwing 2nd and 3rd circle diseases around for shits and giggles, because well, he's out to play for keeps. It's just that.... Exalted are really fucking hard to kill, and odds are that any exalted who survive would try their best to revive the human race. Dragon blood is so dispersed amongst the human population that pretty much everyone has it, and Lunar and Sidereal exaltations are indestructible and there's no way to catch them. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t know about the blanket statement that they\u2019re indestructible and impossible to catch. Normally, yes, but this is a world ending Primordial we\u2019re talking about here. Solar exaltations have been captured by Sidereals and twisted by the dead Neverborn and the fallen Yozi into new forms. Neither of those things were done by the Primordials during the Great War, but if dead and imprisoned Primordials can do it I have to assume that a living one could potentially find a way. <br /> <br /> The Solars are already half corrupted and also all young with no infrastructure, so it might start with Sidereals or Lunars. Not to say that it will definitely happen, but it\u2019s not a possibility that should be completely dismissed. Not normally a thing to think about because most enemies in Exalted fall SO short of full power war-focused Prinordial that it\u2019s not really worth the effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T08:19:10-08:00","id":1367765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367760#post1367760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh no, rest assured, its quite likely that Rametheus goes around throwing 2nd and 3rd circle diseases around for shits and giggles, because well, he's out to play for keeps. It's just that.... Exalted are really fucking hard to kill, and odds are that any exalted who survive would try their best to revive the human race. Dragon blood is so dispersed amongst the human population that pretty much everyone has it, and Lunar and Sidereal exaltations are indestructible and there's no way to catch them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm totally unsure about this but I believe your use of swear words is not a good idea on this forum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T08:36:06-08:00","id":1367773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367765#post1367765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm totally unsure about this but I believe your use of swear words is not a good idea on this forum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Swearing is permitted on the forum when it doesn't break forum rules. For example, you can respect the conversation while swearing; &quot;I think your idea's damn awesome,&quot; for example, but if you say &quot;Shit, this discussion's not worth my time,&quot; that's disrespecting the conversation and thus against the rules.<br /> <br /> \u200b&quot;Fuck yeah,&quot; <b><i>not </i></b>&quot;fuck you.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-14-2020, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T12:53:01-08:00","id":1367836,"title":"","content":"Can I get a Hell Yeah?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T13:14:58-08:00","id":1367843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367836#post1367836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I get a Hell Yeah?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell yeah!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T16:44:53-08:00","id":1367918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367412#post1367412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apologize.<br /> <br /> What I meant was... Well, it's Ramethus. The Garden of War.<br /> <br /> What kind of vulnerability would he have?</div> </div> </div> </div>How about something like this?<br /> <br /> <b>Attrition is Life</b><br /> Cost: 1bhl or 1lhl or 1ahl (+4m, +8m)<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Duration: 1 tick<br /> Keywords: Combo-OK<br /> Pre-reqs: Ramethus Cosmic Principle<br /> <br /> When Ramethus is engaged in Mass Combat and would take damage, Ramethus may pay one health level to prevent that damage completely as a Perfect Defense. Paying with a Bashing level prevents all Bashing damage, and renders Ramethus immune to Bashing damage for the tick (including sub-type damage, such as Stunning damage). A Lethal level does the same for Lethal and Bashing damage. An Aggravated level renders Ramethus immune to all damage for one tick. The cost of this Charm counts as a unique Flaw of Invulnerabiltiy.<br /> <br /> If not in Mass Combat, but rolled into battle with Join Battle, Ramethus may pay a 4m surcharge to use this Charm to become immune to damage, and may reflexively force all combatants to roll Join War, converting the fight to Mass Combat.<br /> <br /> Outside of combat entirely, Ramethus may pay an 8m surcharge to use this Charm against any source of damage.<br /> <br /> <b>War is the Crucible</b><br /> Cost: 0m (+4m, +8m, +12m)<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Keywords: Combo-OK<br /> Pre-reqs: Attrition is Life<br /> <br /> When Ramethus is engaged in Mass Combat, Ramethus may pay 0m to perfectly defend against any effect that would make The Garden of War less effective at combat (apart from health track damage). Such effects include, but are not limited to, Shaping effects, Crippling effects, Compulsion or Servitude effects, and natural or unnatural social influence aimed at convincing Ramethus to stop hostilities. Effects which Ramethus does not defend against (See Unstoppable Force, Immovable Object) and effects which do not reduce Ramethus's combat ability are not valid.<br /> <br /> This Charm may be employed for a +4m surcharge if Ramethus is rolled into battle with Join Battle, or an +8m surcharge if not in combat at all.<br /> <br /> Canny opponents can try to couch their effects in the trappings of war: Ramethus may freely ignore desperate pleas for mercy, but formal calls for cease-fire are a part and parcel of warfare. Defending against attacks stunted as a normal part of warfare carries an additional +4m surcharge, and likely requires Ramethus to spend Willpower and take Limit act against his Intimacy towards Warfare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T11:30:14-07:00","id":1391005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1367695#post1367695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yup. But note, you can't destroy them. And no matter what happened, you can't deal with the fact that exaltation requires free will.<br /> <br /> In other words, exaltation will always be there. Always existing. By all means, lock them away in the deepest, darkest dungeon and throw away the key. There's always the chance they'll get out. And they'll be waiting there for one more spark of heroism to ignite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it was canonically stated in several books that they were lost splats of exalted along with their incarnas in the primordial war, erradicated without a trace- (the number is undisclosed tho, I remember this clearly because the manual of exalted power:infernals is one of those books, not the only one tho.)<br /> <br /> So we have precedents of exaltations being destroyed.<br /> <br /> Nothing should be plain impossible in exalted outside time travel and resurrection.<br /> <br /> Exaltations have been caged before (jade prison) and heavily altered before (lunar shards by the wild, solar shards by neverborn and yozis)<br /> <br /> Altering, caging or destroying shards should be an epic endeavor, like killing or redeeming yozis or incarnaes, but it shouldn't be impossible, it has been done before, and it should be possible to do it again.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12829-tzimiscelord","name":"Tzimiscelord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T13:18:38-07:00","id":1391032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tzimiscelord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391005#post1391005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, it was canonically stated in several books that they were lost splats of exalted along with their incarnas in the primordial war, erradicated without a trace- (the number is undisclosed tho, I remember this clearly because the manual of exalted power:infernals is one of those books, not the only one tho.)<br /> <br /> So we have precedents of exaltations being destroyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's assuming the lost Exalted had an immortal essence that always moves to a new host like Solar Exalted do, it's quite possible they had a more finite one like Dragon-Blooded and Alchemicals do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T13:48:10-07:00","id":1391040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391032#post1391032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's assuming the lost Exalted had an immortal essence that always moves to a new host like Solar Exalted do, it's quite possible they had a more finite one like Dragon-Blooded and Alchemicals do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its a pretty safe assumption.<br /> We know those exalts were empowered by GODS.<br /> ALL exalted empowered by gods had immortal essences, only the &quot;primordial-empowered&quot; ones had a physical and perishable ones.<br /> <br /> Knowing that they were empowered by gods like the solars, lunars and sidereals were and not by primordials like the DBs and alchemicals, immortal essences is the safest bet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12829-tzimiscelord","name":"Tzimiscelord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T14:06:02-07:00","id":1391042,"title":"","content":"Agree to disagree.<br /> If we're thinking about what's potentially missing from the Exalted host in the context of it being &quot;the army of the gods&quot; it's not more command staff and specialists.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T14:12:09-07:00","id":1391043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391042#post1391042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agree to disagree.<br /> If we're thinking about what's potentially missing from the Exalted host in the context of it being &quot;the army of the gods&quot; it's not more command staff and specialists.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What they were isn't relevant to the matter at hand, what I said was just an example that &quot;impossible&quot; is a very flexible term in exalted, and that caging, altering or destroying exaltations shouldn't be 100% off-limits, just being extremely difficult. I just used examples of such instances from the past. The &quot;function&quot; of those exact splats couldn't be more irrelevant for my point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12829-tzimiscelord","name":"Tzimiscelord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T15:07:38-07:00","id":1391057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tzimiscelord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391040#post1391040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Its a pretty safe assumption.<br /> We know those exalts were empowered by GODS.<br /> ALL exalted empowered by gods had immortal essences, only the &quot;primordial-empowered&quot; ones had a physical and perishable ones.<br /> <br /> Knowing that they were empowered by gods like the solars, lunars and sidereals were and not by primordials like the DBs and alchemicals, immortal essences is the safest bet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exigents don't generally have immortal essences, I think.<br /> Seems quite possible that the reason Solars and Lunars and Sidereals survived and the others didn't, is because those three had immortal essences and the others didn't. (Also Alchemicals because you just build new ones, and Dragonblood because there's so damn many.)<br /> <br /> Saying this, I sort of agree with your original point, in that I think that it should be kind of possible in a campaign with some really weird and apocalyptic magic. Though, as with the Yozis escaping Malfeas (which I think can be a fun campaign) I can understand why the writers say canonically it can't happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T15:14:04-07:00","id":1391059,"title":"","content":"I read exalted 3rd edition character creation and charm section and vowed never to buy the book, everything i said i said talking about 2e books and 2e lore.<br /> <br /> In that lore, the exigents does not exist, so the missing incarna and splats must be &quot;normal&quot; 2e shards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12829-tzimiscelord","name":"Tzimiscelord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T16:07:26-07:00","id":1391067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tzimiscelord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391059#post1391059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that lore, the exigents does not exist, so the missing incarna and splats must be &quot;normal&quot; 2e shards.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's headcanon. I follow your reasoning but it's still headcanon because 2e never set down rules for what kind of Exaltation a particular being could make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T16:38:14-07:00","id":1391069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391067#post1391067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that's headcanon. I follow your reasoning but it's still headcanon because 2e never set down rules for what kind of Exaltation a particular being could make.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Occams razor. The simplest answer tends to be the correct one.<br /> <br /> True, we have nothing confirmed or set in stone, but it's far more simple and far more possible for those missing god-powered exaltations to be like every single canon god-powered exaltation, that for them to be a one-of-a-kind unprecedented exception and resemble those who weren't empowered by the gods, but by other beings.<br /> <br /> The fact that neither of those two assumptions are canonically confirmed or denied doesn't make them equally probable.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12829-tzimiscelord","name":"Tzimiscelord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T17:33:33-07:00","id":1391078,"title":"","content":"Occams razor is how I got there too.<br /> Based on the accounts of the Primordial War we have in 2e, if any Exalt type would be singled out for permanent destruction it would be the Solar Exalted because they were the ones actually killing them, but there's no asymmetry in their numbers (both with castes or compared to Lunars) to suggest they ever succeeded in permanently removing one from play. So the missing Exalts were either A. a greater priority to destroy than the Solars despite all evidence to the contrary, or B. easier to destroy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T19:03:32-07:00","id":1391097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tzimiscelord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391069#post1391069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Occams razor. The simplest answer tends to be the correct one.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I don't know because there\u2019s insufficient evidence to reach a certain conclusion&quot; <i>is</i> the simplest answer and makes the fewest assumptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-23-2020, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T01:37:42-07:00","id":1391146,"title":"","content":"I think also, there was (in 2e) 3 kinds of immortal Exalt essences, and 1 kind that wasn't. That's not so different in numbers that you necessarily should assume that everyone who wasn't a Dragonblod was a Celestial that worked the same way as the others (whereas if there was 10 types of Celestial and 1 Terrestrial, you'd assume the Terrestrials were very unusual).<br /> <br /> Actually, I've always found it odd that there's a group name for Solars/Lunars/Sidereals, and a group name for Dragonblood. Why have a group name for a group of 1? I mean, not impossible, I could see scholars doing it. But it does seem likely to me that at least some of the permanently destroyed kinds of Exalts were Terrestrrial, hence a group name for Dragonblood and 1+ other types.<br /> <br /> (In 3e, you've also got Liminals which are Terrestrial, but they didn't exist in the Primordial War.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Though I should say, while I'm disagreeing with Tzimiscelord's reasoning here, I'm still good with their original point of having a game where destroying Celestial essences permanently is a thing that can happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T03:23:22-07:00","id":1391154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tzimiscelord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391059#post1391059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read exalted 3rd edition character creation and charm section and vowed never to buy the book, everything i said i said talking about 2e books and 2e lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're missing out.<br /> <br /> 3E is a very different game to 2E, and the Corebook is easily the worst book (not counting The Solar Novella). But it's a really fun game... and kinda the default assumption. I'm not saying you can't go to a Piston's forum and talk about the 1998 line-up, or a Diablo 3 forum to talk about Season 13, but most folks are going to be discussing the current season.<br /> <br /> Like... did any 2E book even come out under the OP imprint?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T03:32:26-07:00","id":1391155,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... maybe Masters of Jade? But I don't think so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the Corebook is easily the worst book </div> </div> </div> Yes, though not generally the rules themselves (which would be terminal; there are some rules I don't like such as movement and craft, but generally they're good) so much as the lack of editing, and the charm bloat.<br /> Oh, and and the art. 2nd ed Core is a much nicer looking book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But it's a really fun game </div> </div> </div>I would absolutely not want to play 2nd ed again. Solar fights were slow and dull. (DB fights were okay except when someone suddenly died from Five Dragon Force Blow, although it could still be slow.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T04:40:30-07:00","id":1391161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391078#post1391078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Occams razor is how I got there too.<br /> Based on the accounts of the Primordial War we have in 2e, if any Exalt type would be singled out for permanent destruction it would be the Solar Exalted because they were the ones actually killing them,</div> </div> </div> </div>Strongly disagree. If you are being besieged by X exalt types, all of them very good at what they do and all of them needing each other to work as an effective team, and suddenly, by whatever reason, one/several of those becomes vulnerable, you focus the one you can actually destroy, not those who are going to reincarnate in a blink (by primordial standards)<br /> <br /> It is said that they first destroyed their gods and then the exalts, who were directly affected by it. Maybe it's related, maybe not, but there is nothing in any book pointing that solars were a priority. Not even a little bit.<br /> <br /> Also, given that during much of the war (especially, the beginning of it, the timeframe in which the primordials had their bigger ratio of victories) the primordials didn't even knew that solars could kill them, is not that much of an Occam's razor IMO.<br /> The priority can be assigned by a myriad of factors. Even without having the weird lines of thought of the primordials.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391078#post1391078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but there's no asymmetry in their numbers (both with castes or compared to Lunars) to suggest they ever succeeded in permanently removing one from play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely unrelated. Sure, no solars or lunars were destroyed. I never doubted or implied it. <br /> That is an Occam's razor, and <b>I definitely agree with it</b> (it's far more simple and possible that no lunar or solar exaltation was destroyed than having a perfectly symmetrical number of them destroyed.)<br /> That doesn't tell us anything about the lost exalted splats, one way or the other.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391078#post1391078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the missing Exalts were either A. a greater priority to destroy than the Solars despite all evidence to the contrary, or B. easier to destroy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most probably, yeah. Being more vulnerable for whatever reason or circumstance will immediately turn them into a greater priority, and as I said, the altered circumstances after destroying their incarnas may render them easier to destroy. Or it may be part of an elaborate battle plan/circumstances.<br /> <br /> The solar shards were altered into abyssals and infernals and the sidereals and lunar and sidereals didn't because the current circumstances at that moment made them WAY more susceptible to being kidnapped, for example.<br /> Not because the solars were more powerful (that they are, but it wasn\u2019t relevant for that)<br /> <br /> IF instead of having a great chance of corrupting solars the yozis would have had a great opportunity to convert every single dragon blooded instead for whatever reason, they would have taken it too. Same with lunars or sidereals.<br /> <br /> If solar essences were inaccessible and the 300 caged exaltations would have been the lunar ones, they would have gone after those.<br /> <br /> Having a circumstance that greatly benefits something usually make that something into a priority over other courses of action with way less % of success. And especially over things that you cannot do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391097#post1391097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I don't know because there\u2019s insufficient evidence to reach a certain conclusion&quot; <i>is</i> the simplest answer and makes the fewest assumptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s not an answer at all!.<br /> Speculating is one of the best things for me in the exalted fluff (in most fluff actually).<br /> <br /> Trying to think or discover possibilities or alternate ways with fellow fans its fun, and often enlightening. IF you never speculate, you are missing out something great.<br /> Anyways, and while I respect that you don\u2019t want to speculate\u2026..<br /> <br /> Do you really posted here just to say \u201cI don\u2019t know, the book doesn\u2019t say it\u201d?<br /> Would you post that too if someone would have asked what would have happened if chejop had supplanted the empress or if the locust crusade had appeared in the blessed isle?<br /> It contributes nothing to the matter at hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391146#post1391146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think also, there was (in 2e) 3 kinds of immortal Exalt essences, and 1 kind that wasn't. That's not so different in numbers that you necessarily should assume that everyone who wasn't a Dragonblood was a Celestial that worked the same way as the others (whereas if there was 10 types of Celestial and 1 Terrestrial, you'd assume the Terrestrials were very unusual).</div> </div> </div> </div>It sets a very clear tendency. The gods, by preference of necessity, empowered imperishable shards while the primordials, by preference or necessity used physical exaltations that could be destroyed but could be replicated and mass-produced.<br /> <br /> Also you are getting me wrong here. Im not talking about exalted types (celestial and terrestrials), but about the god exalting in shards and the primordials in physical bodies.<br /> <br /> The alchemicals are <b>celestial exalted</b> and they have physical and perishable exaltations, not shards. And they are CELESTIAL. They were just made by a primordial.<br /> Also, terrestrials are more common than every other exalt type combined, I'm not sure I'm getting your point in that line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391146#post1391146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I've always found it odd that there's a group name for Solars/Lunars/Sidereals, and a group name for Dragonblood. Why have a group name for a group of 1? I mean, not impossible, I could see scholars doing it. But it does seem likely to me that at least some of the permanently destroyed kinds of Exalts were Terrestrrial, hence a group name for Dragonblood and 1+ other types.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also unrelated. You have one category for one type of beings with a definite set of characteristics and capabilities and a different one for a being with different capabilities.<br /> Numbers don\u2019t matter.<br /> <br /> Having a group of one is not only common, but logical and normal if they have one or more characteristics that only they have.<br /> <br /> This happens frecuently in botany for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monotypic_taxon\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c1/Leptosomus_discolor_3402120_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monotypic_taxon\" target=\"_blank\"> Monotypic taxon - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monotypic_taxon\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monotypic_taxon </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Numbers are unrelated. You can have 5 taxons with just one specie and one specie only and another taxon with 30 species.<br /> If the celestials can consistently do things the terrestrials cannot, like using celestial martial arts, having better perfects, having higher efficiency charms or (later) having superior type of sorcery, it make sense to separate them in categories, regardless of the number.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391146#post1391146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I should say, while I'm disagreeing with Tzimiscelord's reasoning here, I'm still good with their original point of having a game where destroying Celestial essences permanently is a thing that can happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then please, give me your two cents about how and why we have missing exalted splats after the primordial war. I\u2019m very interested in different points of view and theories. It frequently makes for great histories. (in fact, more often than not, I prefer for people to disagree with me than to agree, I tend to learn much more info that way)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391154#post1391154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're missing out.<br /> <br /> 3E is a very different game to 2E, and the Corebook is easily the worst book (not counting The Solar Novella). But it's a really fun game... and kinda the default assumption. I'm not saying you can't go to a Piston's forum and talk about the 1998 line-up, or a Diablo 3 forum to talk about Season 13, but most folks are going to be discussing the current season.<br /> <br /> Like... did any 2E book even come out under the OP imprint?</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Damn. Maybe I should buy the book and give it a second shot then.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391146#post1391146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would absolutely not want to play 2nd ed again. Solar fights were slow and dull. (DB fights were okay except when someone suddenly died from Five Dragon Force Blow, although it could still be slow.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I must admit I edited the combat system pretty heavily from the beginning. Weapons did far less damage, soak was capped and perfects were 10 motes and 1 WP WAY before 2.5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12829-tzimiscelord","name":"Tzimiscelord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T04:42:12-07:00","id":1391162,"title":"","content":"This is the first time I saw this thread, and its a brilliant idea!<br /> <br /> I was always surprised we never got around to the two missing Primordials either in Canon or with much fan attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T06:44:05-07:00","id":1391182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391162#post1391162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the first time I saw this thread, and its a brilliant idea!<br /> <br /> I was always surprised we never got around to the two missing Primordials either in Canon or with much fan attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh hello, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> ! <br /> <br /> *waves*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T10:20:08-07:00","id":1391209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tzimiscelord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391161#post1391161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s not an answer at all!.</div> </div> </div> </div>To the contrary, &quot;I don't know&quot; is one of the most honest answers a person can give.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tzimiscelord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391161#post1391161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speculating is one of the best things for me in the exalted fluff (in most fluff actually).</div> </div> </div> </div>Speculating is one thing; asserting <i>your</i> speculation over another is a different matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tzimiscelord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391161#post1391161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IF you never speculate, you are missing out something great.<br /> Anyways, and while I respect that you don\u2019t want to speculate\u2026..</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you try not to assume ill intent on my part, please?<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm happy to bounce around ideas.<br /> <br /> Consider for instance, the possibility that the patron that blessed one of these lost Exalt types was neither a god nor the Elemental Dragons, and thus the nature of their relationship to their Exalted champions resembles neither?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tzimiscelord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391161#post1391161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you really posted here just to say \u201cI don\u2019t know, the book doesn\u2019t say it\u201d?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Please read my post a little more charitably.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tzimiscelord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391161#post1391161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you post that too if someone would have asked what would have happened if chejop had supplanted the empress or if the locust crusade had appeared in the blessed isle?</div> </div> </div> </div>If someone else had come forward with a hypothesis out of left field and then tried to claim theirs had the most evidence to warrant it... <b>yes.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tzimiscelord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391161#post1391161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also you are getting me wrong here. Im not talking about exalted types (celestial and terrestrials), but about the god exalting in shards and the primordials in physical bodies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Primordials didn't Exalt people in physical bodies. The Elemental Dragons did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tzimiscelord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391161#post1391161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The alchemicals... were just made by a primordial.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were made by <i>mortals</i>. The electrical impulses running through the nerve of a Primordial gave the Exalted made by mortals a spark of life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-24-2020, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T12:27:51-07:00","id":1391232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391209#post1391209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the contrary, &quot;I don't know&quot; is one of the most honest answers a person can give.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does not contribute anything new or useful to the conversation, so I assumed ill intent. If that was not the case, my sincere apologies. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391209#post1391209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speculating is one thing; asserting <i>your</i> speculation over another is a different matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that several hypotheses can be possible doesn't mean they are equally probable, there is nothing wrong with asserting one speculation over other as long as it's done in good faith, respectfully, and arguing your POV with plausible deductions from the actual canon.<br /> <br /> An entirely different scenario would be to just sink the heels on the ground and doubling down with no proof or act in a disrespectful way, but no one has done that. In this thread at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391209#post1391209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you try not to assume ill intent on my part, please?<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm happy to bounce around ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, my bad, the lack of tone and body language on the internet sometimes let our imaginations fly in a not-so-positive light.<br /> My apologizes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391209#post1391209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consider for instance, the possibility that the patron that blessed one of these lost Exalt types was neither a god nor the Elemental Dragons, and thus the nature of their relationship to their Exalted champions resembles neither?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are explicitly stated to be gods, in the plural. So we know they were several (not only one) and we definitely know they were gods.<br /> <br /> The fact that they were gods doesn't guarantee their exalts have shards like the solar and the lunars, but I genuinely think its the most logical conclusion.<br /> I will never point at it otherwise. I, too, have no ill intent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391209#post1391209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. Please read my post a little more charitably.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, my bad, I will do my best to not let it happen again.<br /> My apologies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391209#post1391209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If someone else had come forward with a hypothesis out of left field and then tried to claim theirs had the most evidence to warrant it... <b>yes.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391209#post1391209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primordials didn't Exalt people in physical bodies. The Elemental Dragons did.<br /> <br /> They were made by <i>mortals</i>. The electrical impulses running through the nerve of a Primordial gave the Exalted made by mortals a spark of life.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'm fairly sure Autobot showed some chemical exalted to the gods as &quot;prototypes&quot;, it ultimately doesn't matter, since my original points was that exaltations made by gods have been destroyed, manipulated and caged before, and thus, it should be possible to do it again in an epic campaign. The rest of my post was just background to that claim.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12829-tzimiscelord","name":"Tzimiscelord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T18:41:55-07:00","id":1391378,"title":"","content":"My memory might be faulty, since it's been years since I looked through DotFA, but I was going with the vague recollection that the reference to the lost Exalt types in it called their patron Incarnae. Note that despite being a Primordial herself, Gaia is mentioned in the 2e core as being an honorary Incarna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T10:32:24-07:00","id":1391508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1391378#post1391378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My memory might be faulty, since it's been years since I looked through DotFA, but I was going with the vague recollection that the reference to the lost Exalt types in it called their patron Incarnae. Note that despite being a Primordial herself, Gaia is mentioned in the 2e core as being an honorary Incarna.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quote from the manual of internals:<br /> <br /> &quot;When the War broke out, the other Primordials rallied<br /> behind their leader. He went from their king to their general.<br /> Early victories against the would-be usurper gods were<br /> due entirely to his might and courage. When the Exalted<br /> rose to strike the hands that had created their world, the<br /> king pulverized and devoured <b>many of the gods</b> who had<br /> empowered them. <b>When those lost Exalted went insane and<br /> turned against one another, the king slaughtered them and<br /> devoured them as well. </b>Yet, the foremost of the Primordials<br /> could not sustain those early victories.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, I think this thread has already had as much useful life as it possibly could unless someone comes with a new and surprising perspective. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12829-tzimiscelord","name":"Tzimiscelord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T18:15:58-07:00","id":1414111,"title":"","content":"I made this thread. <br /> <br /> I claim right of resurrection! <br /> <br /> Elementals, in this shard, are basically animals. Not much different from lightning strikes or tsunamis or clouds. Sometimes, they form after elemental phenomena. Sometimes, they last after the elemental phenomena ends. And, most rare of all, sometimes they retain a sense of self, and become sentient. They have charms based around their element, and as they grow older can expand into bigger, more powerful, and more flexibility. Some mortals, in desperation or greed, bind themselves to the elementals with tattoos and scars of jade, hoping to become the equivalent of Furycrafters.<br /> <br /> Gods in this shard are beings embodied within Creation itself. Their sentience, power, and activity depends on not only their portfolios, as well as how many people worship them. And sometimes, they can be put to sleep or awakened by thaumaturgy and sorcery. A god always has charms befitting their power and their worship. A god of a singular blacksmith's forge can 'transfer' itself to a great steel works with the forge as its beating heart, and gain an increased amount of power due to a large purview and more prayer. A god who has lost their portfolio, like a god of a city that has been wiped out, loses some power... but not all of it. They still hunger for their old positions though, and a god who has lost their city would wish to either take over another one, or recreate it. Gods still gain quintessence and ambrosia, with quintessence based on essence level and ambrosia based on who prays to them. This lets them put out bribes and gifts to gain influence and power.<br /> <br /> Waking up a god is a risky proposition. But a potentially useful one. A god can use their charms to improve a city, or become a tyrannical ruler. Such a thing is never done lightly, and when a god spontaneously gains sentience, religious cults and shrines are erected to keep them propiated. And of course, manipulate and steer them around. Gods don't tend to like other gods. Yes, they enjoy power and allies... but having more gods around means there's less portfolios to snap up, and less prayer to go around.<br /> <br /> There are no gods of universal concepts. There may be a god of a river, who can extend his portfolio over the riverbanks, the rich soil around the riverbanks, and the fish within it... but there is no 'god of rivers'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T15:24:18-07:00","id":1415611,"title":"","content":"Technology should be really, very, varied.<br /> After all, we have people on the same planet typing on an information highway with the sum total of all human knowledge with thinking machines and nano-scale tech, while some people don't have a bathroom and no iron.<br /> And artifacts should reflect that. There should be artifacts made from silk, cloth, plastics, insect shells, wood, porcelain, plastic, the 5MM, amber, bone, ice, gemstones, and everything under the sun.<br /> <br /> ~<br /> <br /> The status of Artifacts and Thaumaturgy and everything else in Creation is a lot different here. For starters, there are more simple artifacts. With the greater tech level and the after-effects of having the Alchemicals and Jadeborn there, the number of artifacts are far, far, greater. Artifacts 3-5 are rare, with N/A being the equivalent of state secrets or secret nuclear launch sites. But the richest of mortals, with Resources 4-5, can afford a jewelled torc or a plate that makes any food place onto it supremely delicious. Every single Dragonblooded scion, with the exception of the rare outcaste, has Artifacts with them. Not so much great storied ones like Volcano cutter, but even the lowest and newest DB has a jadesteel gun with him. <br /> <br /> There's far more thaumaturgy. A rash of sorcerous workings, and the equivalent of missionaries sent out by various DB clans and autochthonian city-states, have led to a profusion of thaumaturgy. Even the smallest and most isolated villages know the bare basics of sanitation and warding against the Fair Folk. At city-centers, where populations congregate and where people search for power, there are sorcerers. Rare amongst the population of mortals, they outnumber the Dragonblooded by a hundred to one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T18:10:14-07:00","id":1416659,"title":"","content":"Information is far more prevalent here, what with the post-apocalyptic bronze age vibe of canon exalted having long since been left behind. Keeping things secret by killing everyone isn't a thing you can do now, not with radio networks, printing presses, and linguistics charms and far greater connectivity to other places, meaning that most information now outraces any attempts to wipe it out. Instead it is dealt with via misinformation campaigns and making sure that there is no secret at all. There may be a secret lab deep within the Denadoro mountains... or it is simply a false trail, meant to exhaust people and resources on a wild goose chase. Yes, there are large lists of demons, as well as many guides on how to summon them. And some of those guides are penned by demon cultists, with specific thaumaturgical rituals built with weaknesses within them, or breeds of demons are created that have a predilection to spout off Yozi rhetoric at inopportune moments. <br /> <br /> Not to say that there aren't trade secrets. The issues of the manifold world means that communication is spotty, and wide-scale networks like the internet are impossible between worlds. Information has to pass via word of mouth, messenger ships, probes, and deliveries of data cassettes. Same thing applies to great Gens of Dragonblooded and Alchemical constructor-cities. Methods of manufacture for various artifacts, potions, medicines, drugs, are trade secrest. As are organisational skills and guidelines. A brisk trade is carried out in the securing and the stealing of such trade secrets using patsies, 3rd parties, and unwitting pawns to carry out their work. Same work goes for sabotage, kidnapping, hijacking certain ships, or just provoking a fair folk attack on an rival's scouting party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}